We need to analyze the problem.

The test scenario:

Frozen journey requirements:
Step 0: seek #shop (likely focusing)
Step 1: press Enter -> expects aria-expanded="true" on #shop and visible #plants (so dropdown opens).
Step 2: seek #search (tab out of navigation to search input) -> expects aria-expanded="false" on #shop and #plants invisible.

Observed failure: At step 2, after tabbing to #search, the assertions fail because aria-expanded on #shop is still "true" (observed true expected false), and #plants visible remains true (should be false).

Thus pressing Tab away from the navigation does not close the dropdown.

In the observed state, we saw sequence of focus events: from body->#home->#contact->#shop (button)->#plants (link inside dropdown?) Actually after pressing Enter on #shop, the focus likely moved to first item in dropdown (#plants). Indeed focusEvents shows: from #shop sequence 3 tag a to #plants. So after opening dropdown, focus moved to #plants (first link). Then subsequent tabs go to #tools, then #search.

But the dropdown remained open when focus left the navigation (i.e., after tabbing from #tools to #search). Expected behavior: when focus leaves the menubar (or navigation) and goes to something else outside the menu, the dropdown should close.

